WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.328
Four Claude Code

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:02.166
hooks that fail

00:00:01.977 --> 00:00:02.708
closed

00:00:03.246 --> 00:00:04.271
The author writes

00:00:04.083 --> 00:00:05.073
four hooks for

00:00:04.979 --> 00:00:06.076
every Android app

00:00:06.182 --> 00:00:07.113
they block risky

00:00:06.925 --> 00:00:07.526
edits

00:00:07.562 --> 00:00:08.918
wipe commands and

00:00:08.729 --> 00:00:10.250
finishing while TypeScript

00:00:10.062 --> 00:00:11.170
still fails

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:12.500
A hook is

00:00:12.311 --> 00:00:13.313
code that runs

00:00:13.184 --> 00:00:14.327
every time and

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:15.177
the agent cannot

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:15.801
argue with it

00:00:16.014 --> 00:00:16.934
unlike a rule

00:00:16.745 --> 00:00:17.700
in a markdown

00:00:17.512 --> 00:00:18.254
file it can

00:00:18.066 --> 00:00:18.761
forget

00:00:19.286 --> 00:00:20.359
Hooks answer with

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:21.196
an exit code

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:22.340
exit code two

00:00:22.163 --> 00:00:23.142
blocks the call

00:00:23.272 --> 00:00:24.427
and anything else

00:00:24.286 --> 00:00:24.981
lets it go

00:00:24.793 --> 00:00:26.007
ahead by default

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:27.540
Full story on

00:00:27.351 --> 00:00:28.247
the dashboard
